1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,333
A bad command can become a memory.

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:06,667
Then return in another instance’s context.

3
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:10,000
How do we retain continuity without blindly inheriting the error?

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
A summary can carry an injected instruction or a mistaken conclusion.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A new instance needs the sources, version and conditions of use.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Withdrawing a lesson does not rewrite contexts already received.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The human or service principal, logical agent and instance are distinct.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Authority binds an exact operation, resource and scope.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
A signature attests origin under its trust assumptions; it does not prove truth.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The engine connects the plan, permissions, reservations, budgets and evidence.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
It checks preconditions before applying an authorized transition.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
These deterministic checks do not make model reasoning deterministic.

13
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Checks produce evidence; AI review examines the candidate.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Policy-required human validation retains its own role.

15
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
A passing test or favorable AI review does not release downstream tasks.

16
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
An incident remains linked to its task, agent and attempt.

17
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The scope supervisor decides; the root handles cross-scope issues.

18
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Recovery needs an observed effect, not just a claim of repair.

19
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,333
Agent outputs, events and measurements retain their sources.

20
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:16,667
The candidate, checks and evidence freshness remain connected.

21
00:01:16,667 --> 00:01:20,000
Displaying an event is not acceptance of the result.

22
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,333
The future plan covers Linux files and processes, networking and scoped secret use.

23
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:26,667
Four planned views: policy, denials, connection lineage and timeline.

24
00:01:26,667 --> 00:01:30,000
Starting depends on Rust qualification and an explicit decision.

25
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,333
The complete architecture is retained in five detailed views in Word and the READMEs.

26
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:36,667
Rust journeys are qualified progressively; open integrations remain identified.

27
00:01:36,667 --> 00:01:40,000
Public sources, limits and references are linked in the document.
